Recommends: mate-panel
Description: screen and keyboard backlight control for the DragonBox Pyra
 The Pyra registers its keyboard light as a backlight device next to the
 screen's. MATE's backlight helper does not recognise either name and takes
 the first one it finds, which is the keyboard, so MATE's brightness applet
 and its idle dimming both adjust the keyboard instead of the screen.
 .
 This package names each device explicitly and sets it through logind, so
 no root is needed:
 .
  * pyra-brightness-applet, a MATE panel applet with a slider for the
    screen and one for the keyboard, usable with the arrow keys
  * pyra-idle-dim, a user service that dims the screen when the session
    goes idle and brings it back on wake
